1
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:29,950
Okay, a skin case. One piece of tissue.

2
00:00:30,100 --> 00:00:31,300
Let me look it over.

3
00:00:36,700 --> 00:00:41,300
Walking along each piece at low power,
confirming the epidermis is intact.

4
00:00:46,600 --> 00:00:49,500
Here are the dermo-epidermal junctions.

5
00:00:49,600 --> 00:00:51,300
Let me work along each one.

6
00:01:12,900 --> 00:01:16,750
Along this junction, I'm flagging 18 foci.

7
00:01:16,900 --> 00:01:20,800
Confluent proliferation, lentiginous proliferation,

8
00:01:21,400 --> 00:01:23,800
junctional nests, melanophages.

9
00:01:30,300 --> 00:01:33,300
Inspecting the dermis here. Give me a sec.

10
00:01:37,400 --> 00:01:39,600
Scanning the dermis under the junction.

11
00:01:43,800 --> 00:01:46,800
Let me follow that down into the dermis underneath.

12
00:01:50,800 --> 00:01:53,600
Looking for mitotic figures down here.

13
00:01:57,200 --> 00:02:00,100
Flagging three possible mitotic figures.

14
00:02:04,100 --> 00:02:05,900
That's my read of this one.

15
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:07,900
Handing control back to you.
